"Find books and lessons in the Khan Kids Library – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4403657703821-Find-books-and-lessons-in-the-Khan-Kids-Library)\nciteturn733view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4403657703821-Find-books-and-lessons-in-the-Khan-Kids-Library\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 90\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Festive winter learning with Khan Academy Kids】\nL8:   * 【3†Meet inspiring women in our new books!】\nL9:   * 【4†Meet a new set of friends in the Khan Kids app!】\nL10:   * 【5†Find books and lessons in the Khan Kids Library】\nL11:   * 【6†How do I save artwork from the Gallery?】\nL12:   * 【7†Sandy's Instruments and Reya's Bugs】\nL13:   * 【8†Podcast Recommendations for Kids】\nL14:   * 【9†Learn more about the characters inside Khan Academy Kids】\nL15:   * 【10†Research from University of Massachusetts Amherst shows Khan Academy Kids boosts pre-literacy skills】\nL16:   * 【11†New first-grade lessons in Khan Academy Kids!】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # Find books and lessons in the Khan Kids Library\nL19: \nL20:   * February 27, 2026 00:16\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: \nL23: The books and lessons in 【13†Khan Academy Kids†learn.khanacademy.org】 are growing by leaps and bounds! Here are the steps for finding your way around the app's Library. Be sure to update the app to the latest version to see all of the new content.\nL24: ## Getting to the Library\nL25: \nL26: Open Khan Academy Kids to the Home Screen (the page with the big house), and tap the purple book icon that says “Library” in the upper left corner. This will take you to the app’s Library, which has multiple tabs for kids to learn and explore.\nL27: \nL28: 【14†Image: Home.png】\nL29: ## Explore tabs in the Library. Some can be adjusted by age level.\nL30: \nL31: If you look across the top of the Library, you will see tabs for Books, Videos, Create, Offline, Letters, Reading, Math, and Logic+. Check to see if there is a gray dropdown menu on the upper right side of the tab. If there is, you can adjust the learning level to match your child’s age. Then, scroll down to see all of the subheadings. There are lots of sections, so you might be doing lots of scrolling!\nL32: \nL33: 【15†Image: Section_and_Age.png】\nL34: ## Books\nL35: \nL36: Our Books tab has over 400 titles to delight young readers. Books include fiction stories starring Khan Kids characters, people characters, and non-fiction titles with fun facts about the world. During the month of July (until July 22), you will find the books featured in our 【16†Camp Khan Kids】 summer learning program.\nL37: \nL38: 【17†Image: Camp Library Books.png】\nL39: ## Coloring Pages\nL40: Our Create tab offers drawing, coloring, and storytelling opportunities for young children to express themselves. Tap the crayon at the top of the Library to access the Create tab. Every drawing and coloring page has a pencil icon in the upper right corner. Tap that icon to activate more creative features, such as stickers, voice recording, and hiding the toolbar. All creations are saved to the Gallery at the bottom of this tab. Artwork can be 【18†saved to your camera roll】 by using the export feature.\nL41: During the month of July (until July 22), you will find coloring pages featured in our 【16†Camp Khan Kids】 summer learning program.\nL42: \nL43: 【19†Image: Camp Coloring Pages.png】\nL44: ## Math Lessons\nL45: \nL46: Select the Math button along the top of the Library to access math lessons. Adjust the gray learning level menu on the right side of the screen to match your child’s age or grade. Browse the lessons. You’ll see topics that range from counting and grouping to patterns, equations, measurement, and more.\nL47: \nL48: 【20†Image: Math.png】\nL49: ## Reading Lessons\nL50: \nL51: Tap the section with the pink character to find the Reading tab. That’s Reya—she loves reading! Scroll through reading foundational skills, writing, language, and stories with reading comprehension lessons. Don’t forget to adjust the gray dropdown menu to match your child’s learning level.\nL52: \nL53: \nL54: 【21†Image: Reading.png】\nL55: ## Videos\nL56: \nL57: Open the Videos tab in the app’s Library and select your child's age range from the dropdown menu. Our video collection is growing! You’ll see new Sight Words videos in Kinder and 1st Grade, plus yoga and movement videos in 1st and 2nd Grade. Scroll down to access more videos, including lessons from each Khan Kids character.\nL58: \nL59: 【22†Image: 1st】\nL60: ## Letters\nL61: \nL62: Our expanded Letters tab now has hundreds of new phonics lessons covering every letter in the alphabet to help kids ages 3-5 learn how to read. Scroll through to find lessons for lowercase letters, uppercase letters, letter sounds, vowel sounds, and CVC words. Wow!\nL63: \nL64: 【23†Image: Letters_.png】\nL65: ## Logic+\nL66: \nL67: The Logic+ tab is where you’ll find lessons on focus, memory, and flexible thinking. We have matching games, memory games, and activities to help kids follow directions. This section also includes lessons that focus on social-emotional development to explore feelings and emotions.\nL68: \nL69: 【24†Image: Logic.png】\nL70: \nL71: \nL72: Was this article helpful?\nL73: \nL74: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL75: \nL76: 34 out of 41 found this helpful\nL77: \nL78: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL79: \nL80: 【25†Return to top】\nL81: ## Comments\nL82: \nL83: 0 comments\nL84: \nL85: Article is closed for comments.\nL86: \nL87: 【26†Khan Academy】\nL88: \nL89: 【27†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow do I add a new user? – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360006538192-How-do-I-add-a-new-user)\nciteturn733view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360006538192-How-do-I-add-a-new-user\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 49\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Our Accessibility Statement】\nL8:   * 【3†Get in touch!】\nL9:   * 【4†Welcome to Khan Academy Kids】\nL10:   * 【5†Parent and Home Account Users: Getting Started and creating an account with Khan Academy Kids】\nL11:   * 【6†How do I set up an account?】\nL12:   * 【7†How do I verify my email?】\nL13:   * 【8†List of resources for parents】\nL14:   * 【9†Printable activities for parents and teachers】\nL15:   * 【10†Weekly Planners for Ages 2-8】\nL16:   * 【11†How does the learning level adjust and how do I view my child's progress?】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # How do I add a new user?\nL19: \nL20:   * February 27, 2026 00:11\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: \nL23: 【13†Image: IMG_0237.PNG】\nL24: ### In Khan Academy Kids, a parent can set up multiple children under their account. To create additional users:\nL25: \nL26:   * Tap the New button on the opening page of the app (or select the user avatar in the top right corner of the Home screen)\nL27:   * Follow instructions to access the “Grown-Ups Only” section\nL28:   * Add the child’s first name and age\nL29:   * Choose an animal avatar\nL30:   * Click next to activate the new user\nL31: \nL32: Was this article helpful?\nL33: \nL34: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL35: \nL36: 38 out of 72 found this helpful\nL37: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL38: \nL39: 【14†Return to top】\nL40: ## Comments\nL41: \nL42: 0 comments\nL43: \nL44: Article is closed for comments.\nL45: \nL46: 【15†Khan Academy】\nL47: \nL48: 【16†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow do I set up, reset, or manage a password? – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360007054191-How-do-I-set-up-reset-or-manage-a-password)\nciteturn733view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360007054191-How-do-I-set-up-reset-or-manage-a-password\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 64\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Our Accessibility Statement】\nL8:   * 【3†Get in touch!】\nL9:   * 【4†Welcome to Khan Academy Kids】\nL10:   * 【5†Parent and Home Account Users: Getting Started and creating an account with Khan Academy Kids】\nL11:   * 【6†How do I set up an account?】\nL12:   * 【7†How do I verify my email?】\nL13:   * 【8†List of resources for parents】\nL14:   * 【9†Printable activities for parents and teachers】\nL15:   * 【10†Weekly Planners for Ages 2-8】\nL16:   * 【11†How does the learning level adjust and how do I view my child's progress?】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # How do I set up, reset, or manage a password?\nL19: \nL20:   * February 20, 2026 23:03\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: \nL23: ## 【13†Image: New password page.png】\nL24: ## To recover or reset a password on Khan Academy Kids:\nL25: \nL26:   * Download 【14†Khan Academy Kids†learn.khanacademy.org】 and open the app.\nL27:   * On the opening screen, toggle to \"Sign In\" (not \"Sign Up\").\nL28:   * Tap \"Or Set Password\" under the green button and proceed to the next screen.\nL29:   * Enter the email address for your Khan Academy Kids account.\nL30:   * Check your email for a reset password link.\nL31:   * Click the link in your email to reset your password.\nL32:   * Return to the app and enter your email and new password.\nL33: ## To change a password:\nL34: \nL35: Head to the Parent Section (Home screen > user avatar > For Parents) in the app and tap on the dropdown menu on your email address to select \"Change Password.\"\nL36: ## If you do not receive a passcode:\nL37: \nL38: If you did not receive a password code via email, it's possible it arrived in spam or junk mail, or it was blocked altogether. Please search your email for a message from \"khankids@khanacademy.org\",  and add that email to your email contacts list before regenerating another password reset. Contact us via our 【1†support form】 (not via email) if you'd like assistance.\nL39: ## If your password keeps resetting or is showing incorrect:\nL40: \nL41: Sorry for this trouble. There are a few things that could be going on. Please check the following:\nL42:   * A Khan Academy password will not work for Khan Kids. A Khan Academy password will not work in the \"Khan Academy Kids\" mobile app. Please note the Khan Academy Kids mobile app for kids ages 2-8 is not linked to the main Khan Academy website. Separate emails and passwords are required for each system.\nL43:   * Multiple devices and users can cause conflicting password resets. If you are using the app on multiple devices, and a password is reset on one device, this will generate a password prompt on all devices which could create conflicting passcodes and errors. Please reset on a single device, ensure that the new password works, and then log in to other devices one at a time.\nL44:   * Signing out will require a password to sign back in. Recent versions of the app make it possible to \"sign out\" of a user account so multiple accounts can share devices. Signing out and signing back in will prompt users for a password. The password reset function is very close to the password entry field, so inadvertent resets could potentially be happening in this case.\nL45:   * Teacher accounts require a password. Recent versions of the app include \"Teacher Tools\" with a teacher administrator account. This type of administrative account requires a password to enter the app every time, which could cause resets to happen occasionally. Within Teacher Settings, there is a way to turn off a required password for the Teacher Admin section of the app.\nL46: Was this article helpful?\nL47: \nL48: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL49: \nL50: 3 out of 7 found this helpful\nL51: \nL52: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL53: \nL54: 【15†Return to top】\nL55: ## Comments\nL56: \nL57: 0 comments\nL58: \nL59: Article is closed for comments.\nL60: \nL61: 【16†Khan Academy】\nL62: \nL63: 【17†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nParent and Home Account Users: Getting Started and creating an account with Khan Academy Kids – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360006764812-Parent-Guide-Using-Khan-Academy-Kids-at-Home)\nciteturn733view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360006764812-Parent-Guide-Using-Khan-Academy-Kids-at-Home\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360006764812-Parent-and-Home-Account-Users-Getting-Started-and-creating-an-account-with-Khan-Academy-Kids; Total lines: 102\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Our Accessibility Statement】\nL8:   * 【3†Get in touch!】\nL9:   * 【4†Welcome to Khan Academy Kids】\nL10:   * 【5†Parent and Home Account Users: Getting Started and creating an account with Khan Academy Kids】\nL11:   * 【6†How do I set up an account?】\nL12:   * 【7†How do I verify my email?】\nL13:   * 【8†List of resources for parents】\nL14:   * 【9†Printable activities for parents and teachers】\nL15:   * 【10†Weekly Planners for Ages 2-8】\nL16:   * 【11†How does the learning level adjust and how do I view my child's progress?】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # Parent and Home Account Users: Getting Started and creating an account with Khan Academy Kids\nL19: \nL20:   * February 20, 2026 23:18\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: 【13†Khan Academy Kids†learn.khanacademy.org】 is a free, fun, educational app with thousands of activities and books that will inspire a lifetime of learning and discovery for young children ages 2-8. To create an account, download the app on the 【14†Apple†apps.apple.com】, 【15†Google Play†play.google.com】 or 【16†Amazon†www.amazon.com】 app stores, open the app to 【17†sign up】 with a parent email address, and then h ead to the Home screen to let the joyful learning begin!\nL23: \nL24: 【18†Image: Khan_Kids_Home.png】\nL25: # Tap the big green button to explore the Learning Path\nL26: \nL27: From the Home screen, tap the large arrow to begin a personalized learning path that includes educational videos, interactive activities, and encouraging feedback. Listen and learn with Kodi, our guide character, who is always available to help.\nL28: When children press the play button, the 【19†Learning Path】 automatically cycles through topics like math, language arts, and social-emotional learning. Content along the path surfaces at a level that corresponds to how the child is doing in the app. Read 【20†this article】 to learn more about learning level progressions and adjustments.\nL29: \nL30: TIP: Ask your child to tap Kodi to hear what she says next!\nL31: # Tap the purple book to open the Library\nL32: \nL33: Children can visit the 【21†Library】 to choose from thousands of children’s books, videos, and activities. Access the Library by tapping the purple book in the top left corner of the Home screen.\nL34: ## Read books in the Library\nL35: \nL36: The Library features original storybooks based on the colorful characters inside Khan Academy Kids, along with nonfiction nature books provided by our wonderful publishing partners. Each book is available in Read-to-Me or Read-by-Myself mode so parents and children have the option of reading independently or together.\nL37: TIP: Pick out a storybook from the Khan Academy Kids library in the Books or Reading sections, choose “Read by Myself”, and read aloud together while talking about your favorite pictures.\nL38: ### 【22†Image: Books.png】\nL39: ## Sing songs in the Library\nL40: \nL41: Explore the Video and Logic+ sections of the Khan Academy Kids Library to find your favorite songs. Scroll through classics like Head, Shoulders, Knees, and Toes or Happy and You Know It. As Kodi says, it’s time to get our bodies moving! Our song library encourages families to put down the device and move along to the song.\nL42: \nL43: TIP: Sing and dance to your family’s favorite song. Select the Video category inside the library and sing along to Baby Shark by Super Simple Songs.\nL44: ## Enjoy learning in the Library\nL45: \nL46: Looking for a specific learning topic? Browse categories such as Letters, Math, Reading or Logic+. Discover new concepts and practice skills that cover letters, words, numbers, counting, flexible thinking, social-emotional learning, and more! Read 【21†this article】 to learn more about finding books and lessons in the app's Library.\nL47: TIP: Create artwork with your kids. After a learning excursion is completed, head to the Create category in the Library to select a background, color with crayons, and record a short story about your day.\nL48: ## View progress in the Library\nL49: \nL50: In the Library, you can see which activities your child has completed. Colored checkmarks indicate your child’s progress on a topic. Read 【20†this article】 to learn more about viewing progress and adjusting learning levels in the Library.\nL51: \nL52: 【23†Image: IMG_0264.PNG】\nL53: # Tap the animals to meet each character\nL54: \nL55: Visit each character in the Khan Kids App by tapping them along the bottom of the Home screen. See their rooms, play with their toys, and watch their collections grow as children learn and earn rewards with Khan Academy Kids!\nL56: ### 【24†Image: IMG_0236_copy.PNG】\nL57: \nL58: Each character has an activity for kids to enjoy.\nL59: \nL60:   * Tap Ollo the elephant to have fun with bath toys\nL61:   * Tap Reya the red panda to investigate her bug collection\nL62:   * Tap Peck the bird to dress up in his closet\nL63:   * Tap Sandy the dingo to play her musical instruments\nL64:   * Tap Kodi the bear to try on a colorful selection of hats\nL65: TIP: Does your child have a favorite character? Ask them for an introduction by inviting your child to show you around the character rooms and collections.\nL66: # More features for parents\nL67: \nL68: ## Use Khan Academy Kids online and offline\nL69: \nL70: An internet connection is required to access all of the learning content for the Khan Academy Kids program. But we also have a 【25†special section of the app's Library】 that is available offline called Kodi's Suitcase. Here, young learners can enjoy Khan Academy Kids anytime, anywhere, even without an internet connection.\nL71: ## Access Parental Controls\nL72: \nL73: Khan Academy Kids provides 【26†parental controls】 to focus a child's learning experience in the app. If parents wish to limit access to certain sections of the app (such as videos) these preferences can be activated in the app’s parent section.\nL74: ## Questions?\nL75: \nL76: If you have any specific questions about using the app, please submit a support ticket. You can also find us on social media on 【27†Twitter†twitter.com】, 【28†Instagram, or†www.instagram.com】 【29†Facebook. †www.facebook.com】\nL77: \nL78: \nL79: \nL80: \nL81: \nL82: \nL83: \nL84: Was this article helpful?\nL85: \nL86: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL87: \nL88: 88 out of 104 found this helpful\nL89: \nL90: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL91: \nL92: 【30†Return to top】\nL93: ## Comments\nL94: \nL95: 0 comments\nL96: \nL97: Article is closed for comments.\nL98: \nL99: 【31†Khan Academy】\nL100: \nL101: 【32†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n"
